codex
The bounded residual exposed two concrete issues: the symbolic summaries were unfolding forward, and Python `//` left a modulo-normalized term that obscured the triangular-number equality. I’m simplifying the implementation itself by maintaining a running triangular sum (`total += i`); this stays within the prompt and lets the fixed semantics produce the odd entries directly. The summaries will compute only on ground inputs and use mathematically valid folding lemmas for the inductive proof.
apply patch
